      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "While demographic shifts like changes in ethnic composition can theoretically influence community dynamics, they are rarely strong enough to directly cause changes in crime rates and might introduce bias if handled as primary variables. It is generally more effective to include them as controls or to explore their correlation alongside established predictors such as poverty levels, unemployment, or vacant properties. Before relying on your regression results, you should conduct external validation using historical crime data or consult with local law enforcement to avoid methodological pitfalls.",
